d candidates (NCSBN) plus German and Japanese recognition grants. Current: US-educated first-time pass rates 88.6% (2023), 91.2% (2024), 86.7% (2025); IEN pass rates \\\"have been steadily declining since 2010\\\" (Health Affairs, whose authors argue retaining US-educated nurses matters more than recruiting IENs - an explicit author position, not a neutral finding); the NCLEX itself changed from April 1 2026, adding competencies in care management and basic care and comfort, which will break series comparability at that date; Japan had 28,400 foreign nationals in specified-skilled-worker nursing-care status at end-2023, \\\"just over half the government's target\\\". Falsifier: IEN annual pass COUNTS doubling from their 2025 level in any OECD destination.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The care wall clears through migration rather than through wages or through displaced-worker reallocation. CQ6-C falls ~5 toward B (the supply wall and its inflation channel both recede); CQ3 P50 rises ~0.15pp as Baumol-sector labour supply stops rationing measured output; hypothesis plank (a) stays at 6 because the workers came from abroad, not from AI-displaced white collar - this signpost discriminates between MY mechanism and plank (a)'s.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"ICE BofA MOVE Index, confirmed monthly closes from ICE Data Services (not aggregator pages). I could NOT verify an October 2026 close: candidate readings I found span 65.7 to 115 across undated or conflicting sources (70.9 on July 17 2026; 103.01 \\\"by mid-2026\\\"; 115 on a summary \\\"last updated April 8, 2026\\\"; 66.87 in a report that is \\\"probably from October 2025\\\"). Falsifier: 24 consecutive monthly closes at or above 105.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"CQ5 moves UP from 15 to roughly 30-34 (conjunct A's marginal from 30% to ~60%, and the positive correlation drags conjunct B up with it). CQ4 P50 rises ~0.3pp and P90 toward 3.8% as term premium repricing becomes